; Regression: a returned value must conform to the DECLARED return type
; (2026-08-27).
;
; Nothing asked. `current_return_type` and the binding/`set` target types were
; only ever READ -- for the literal retype, the char/float fold, the cstr wrap,
; the tail promotion and the three `ref` gates -- and never used as an
; ACCEPTOR, while types_compatible# ran at ten sites, every one of them a
; PARAMETER. So `return` was unchecked in both directions, silently: measured
; on the untouched tree, `returns ref[Alpha]?` with `return x` for an
; `x: ref[Beta]` emitted `ret ptr %0`, two unrelated concepts confused outright
; at rc 0.
;
; The exit is that there ISN'T one for this shape -- the declaration is simply
; wrong. What the check must keep accepting is in type_conformance_ok.scaly.
;
; xfail: does not conform to the declared type

define Alpha (a: int)
define Beta (b: int)

function pick(x: ref[Beta]) returns ref[Alpha]?
{
    return x
}

var b Beta(7)
let r pick(&b)
Console.println "unreachable"
